      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Cirques, Arêtes, and Horns are classic erosional landforms produced exclusively by glacial action.",
        "Barchans are crescent-shaped sand dunes formed by wind deposition, with horns pointing in the direction of the wind.",
        "Ox-bow lakes, alluvial fans, and deltas are key river (fluvial) depositional features frequently asked in geography MCQs."
      ],
