    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Rivers carve steep V-shaped valleys, gorges, and waterfalls through vertical and lateral fluvial erosion.",
        "Glaciers reshape landscapes into U-shaped valleys, cirques, hanging valleys, and moraines via plucking and abrasion.",
        "Wind acts as the primary geomorphic agent in arid regions, shaping landforms like yardangs, mushroom rocks, and barchans.",
        "Understanding the distinction between erosional and depositional features of each agent is crucial for physical geography."
